WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.529
Is there anything worse than your favorite
TV show coming to an end?

00:00:03.529 --> 00:00:07.480
Well, there is, actually: when that show still
had a lot of life left in it and should never

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:09.180
have been cancelled in the first place.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:13.190
It's one thing when a show reaches the end
of its natural life cycle and rides off into

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:14.190
the sunset.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.780
But it's another when that show is murdered
by the network.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.670
"I have a terrible idea."

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:23.320
Here's a look at five TV show cancellations
that were a mistake.

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:24.430
Bloodline

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:31.039
With an all-star cast including Kyle Chandler,
Sissy Spacek, and Linda Cardellini, Bloodline

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:34.059
was touted as the next big prestige series
from Netflix.

00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:39.390
Instead, it got a pink slip after just three
seasons despite increasing buzz, including

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.940
an Emmy win and Golden Globe nomination for
co-star Ben Mendelsohn.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:48.219
Since Netflix rarely releases any of their
viewership statistics, it's impossible to

00:00:48.219 --> 00:00:52.900
know how many fans the show actually has,
but rumors claim the series was yanked as

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:57.399
part of a financial dispute between Netflix
and Sony, which produced the series.

00:00:57.399 --> 00:01:01.879
Whatever the reason, it's too bad this Bloodline
has gone extinct.

00:01:01.879 --> 00:01:03.629
Marvel's Agent Carter

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:08.060
While Marvel's movies have been hitting on
all cylinders, their TV shows have had a spottier

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.060
record.

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:13.029
That's what makes it even more tragic that
arguably their best show yet, Marvel's Agent

00:01:13.029 --> 00:01:17.380
Carter, was cancelled after just two short
seasons, ending on a cliffhanger that may

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.060
never be resolved.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.740
"I'm leaving just give me a second."

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.999
Who shot him?

00:01:25.999 --> 00:01:26.999
Is he okay?

00:01:26.999 --> 00:01:27.999
What's happening?

00:01:27.999 --> 00:01:28.999
We may never know.

00:01:28.999 --> 00:01:33.329
And the show's untimely demise was especially
galling considering the series was not just

00:01:33.329 --> 00:01:38.350
a critical darling, but vital to building
the backstory of the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:42.259
giving fans a look at all the events that
shaped the superhero world from the end of

00:01:42.259 --> 00:01:44.969
World War II through the debut of Iron Man.

00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:49.679
With decades of stories still untold, here's
hoping Marvel gives Agent Carter another chance

00:01:49.679 --> 00:01:51.719
some time in the future.

00:01:51.719 --> 00:01:53.549
Good Girls Revolt

00:01:53.549 --> 00:01:58.819
Quick history lesson: back in 1983, a new
sitcom called Cheers was among the lowest

00:01:58.819 --> 00:02:00.570
rated shows on television.

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:05.649
Rather than cancel it, though, NBC decided
to give it a chance to build a fanbase, resulting

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:08.489
in one of the most beloved runs in television
history.

00:02:08.489 --> 00:02:11.409
Cheers thrived because it was given time to
mature.

00:02:11.409 --> 00:02:16.420
But no such opportunity was given to the Amazon
series Good Girls Revolt, which was amazingly

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:22.469
cancelled just six weeks after the first season
debuted in October, 2016, far too soon for

00:02:22.469 --> 00:02:26.870
the streaming service to know whether or not
its story about women seeking equal rights

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:29.020
in the late '60s would catch on with viewers.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:34.220
"Some of the other girls and I, are filing
an Equal Employment Claim.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.359
It's illegal for them not to let us write.

00:02:36.359 --> 00:02:38.379
And we want the policy changed."

00:02:38.379 --> 00:02:39.870
So why the quick hook?

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:45.439
According to reports, Amazon Studios chief
Roy Price personally disliked the show, even

00:02:45.439 --> 00:02:47.890
though it apparently was popular with viewers.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.390
He gets a vote.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.709
Fans don’t.

00:02:50.709 --> 00:02:52.079
The Nightly Show

00:02:52.079 --> 00:02:58.030
When Stephen Colbert left his Comedy Central
hit The Colbert Report in 2015, veteran Daily

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:02.909
Show contributor Larry Wilmore took over the
time slot with his own spin on the events

00:03:02.909 --> 00:03:04.930
of the day, The Nightly Show.

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:08.439
And his take on things was one many viewers
felt was long overdue.

00:03:08.439 --> 00:03:12.629
"And hearing from you guys has been incredible.

00:03:12.629 --> 00:03:15.290
Even you, @Wilmore_blows666"

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:20.500
Unfortunately, Wilmore's dry humor and incisive
look at political and social issues didn't

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.230
draw high enough ratings to satisfy the network.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:27.920
The good news is, Wilmore has since signed
a development deal with ABC, but in today's

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:32.159
divisive political climate, his voice is sorely
missed.

00:03:32.159 --> 00:03:33.329
BrainDead

00:03:33.329 --> 00:03:38.519
This science-fiction-horror-political satire-comedy
was probably a bit of a risk for CBS.

00:03:38.519 --> 00:03:43.980
But it had a nice pedigree going for it: It
was created by Michelle and Robert King, creators

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:47.290
of CBS's long-running legal drama The Good
Wife.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:51.730
The offbeat premise: A documentary filmmaker
from a prominent family goes to work for her

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:57.499
senator brother in Washington, D.C. and discovers
that parasitic alien bugs taken over the minds

00:03:57.499 --> 00:03:59.489
of the U.S. government's top leaders.

00:03:59.489 --> 00:04:03.810
The show was canceled because of low ratings,
probably because people are just getting tired

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:04.999
of reality television.

00:04:04.999 --> 00:04:06.519
Thanks for watching!

00:04:06.519 --> 00:04:09.129
